1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,340
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,340 --> 00:00:04,780
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:05,970
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,290 --> 00:00:07,520
I've been a nursing
assistant

5
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,620
for thirty years.

6
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:10,280
Lifting and turning
patients,

7
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:12,080
bending over beds all
shift.

8
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:13,060
I had my right knee

9
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:14,590
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:14,730 --> 00:00:16,580
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:18,130
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:19,560
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:20,650
and it went away.

14
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:21,860
This is different.

15
00:00:21,930 --> 00:00:22,580
Tight.

16
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:23,300
Full.

17
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:24,260
Like a band around

18
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:26,280
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:27,520
And for two years I've

20
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:28,810
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:29,810
Give it time.

22
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:31,800
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,320
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:34,510
At three months,

25
00:00:34,510 --> 00:00:35,550
give it six.

26
00:00:35,990 --> 00:00:36,900
At six months,

27
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:38,490
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:39,380
At a year,

29
00:00:39,380 --> 00:00:41,460
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:42,800
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:44,090
We went down the list.

32
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:45,520
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:46,830
Every session,

34
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:48,410
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:49,750
I got stronger.

36
00:00:49,790 --> 00:00:51,460
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:52,840
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:54,180
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:56,120
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:57,090
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:57,090 --> 00:00:58,340
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:00:58,430 --> 00:01:00,010
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:01,800
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:01,990 --> 00:01:03,290
And after that, a second

45
00:01:03,290 --> 00:01:04,560
operation to go back

46
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:05,960
in and do it over.

47
00:01:06,330 --> 00:01:07,260
I said no.

48
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,120
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:10,140
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:11,760
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:14,260
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:15,910
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:15,910 --> 00:01:17,500
for it and went to my
shift.

54
00:01:17,570 --> 00:01:18,800
Couldn't do the stairs,

55
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:19,850
couldn't stand at the
counter

56
00:01:19,850 --> 00:01:21,360
long enough to finish
dinner,

57
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:23,030
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

58
00:01:23,030 --> 00:01:24,990
without shifting every two
minutes.

59
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:26,650
At work I couldn't kneel
to put

60
00:01:26,650 --> 00:01:28,410
a resident's shoes on
without grabbing

61
00:01:28,410 --> 00:01:30,040
the bed rail to get back
up.

62
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:31,730
The other aides started
taking

63
00:01:31,730 --> 00:01:32,940
my lifts for me.

64
00:01:33,030 --> 00:01:34,430
It woke me at night,

65
00:01:34,430 --> 00:01:36,430
and it turned ordinary
things,

66
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:37,590
like getting in the car

67
00:01:37,590 --> 00:01:39,100
or up off the couch,

68
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:40,370
into a decision.

69
00:01:40,490 --> 00:01:41,930
After a long and serious

70
00:01:41,930 --> 00:01:43,290
talk with my husband,

71
00:01:43,290 --> 00:01:45,160
I went back in one more
time.

72
00:01:45,490 --> 00:01:46,460
That was the fourth set

73
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:47,980
of X-rays on this knee.

74
00:01:48,190 --> 00:01:49,720
And like the three before
it,

75
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:52,390
the answer was everything
looks great.

76
00:01:52,550 --> 00:01:54,710
No loosening, no
infection,

77
00:01:54,710 --> 00:01:55,830
nothing wrong.

78
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:56,870
Only this time there

79
00:01:56,870 --> 00:01:58,080
was no new number.

80
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:00,380
Nobody said give it
another six months.

81
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,230
There was nothing left to
give it.

82
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:03,280
I sat in the parking

83
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:04,280
lot for a while.

84
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:06,080
Okay, I thought.

85
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:08,030
Then explain this.

86
00:02:08,170 --> 00:02:10,620
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

87
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:12,150
I hit my breaking point.

88
00:02:12,190 --> 00:02:14,160
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

89
00:02:14,310 --> 00:02:16,210
Everyone in the house was
asleep

90
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:17,900
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

91
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:18,970
with my leg up,

92
00:02:18,970 --> 00:02:20,770
trying to find any angle

93
00:02:20,770 --> 00:02:22,040
where it didn't feel like
something

94
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:23,550
was wrapped around my knee

95
00:02:23,550 --> 00:02:24,550
and tightening.

96
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:27,330
I had a shift at seven.

97
00:02:27,490 --> 00:02:30,060
My husband didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

98
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:32,370
By then I'd stopped
telling him.

99
00:02:32,490 --> 00:02:33,550
And I just thought,

100
00:02:33,550 --> 00:02:35,310
is this really my life
now?

101
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:36,900
I can't live like this.

102
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:38,790
So I made myself a
promise.

103
00:02:38,830 --> 00:02:39,740
I wouldn't go a day

104
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:41,440
without looking for an
answer.

105
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:43,000
And when I found one,

106
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,270
I'd share it with everyone

107
00:02:44,270 --> 00:02:45,760
going through the same
thing.

108
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:48,170
So I got my laptop

109
00:02:48,170 --> 00:02:49,510
out and went looking.

110
00:02:49,550 --> 00:02:50,770
Not for a product.

111
00:02:50,810 --> 00:02:52,330
For an explanation.

112
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:54,210
Mayo Clinic forums,

113
00:02:54,210 --> 00:02:56,470
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

114
00:02:56,470 --> 00:02:59,390
doctor videos, medical
animations.

115
00:02:59,670 --> 00:03:00,650
And that's when I found

116
00:03:00,650 --> 00:03:02,580
a video from a physical
therapist

117
00:03:02,580 --> 00:03:03,160
named Dr.

118
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:05,320
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

119
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:07,280
had been through exactly
this.

120
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,920
But before I say anything
else,

121
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,580
I want to be straight with
you.

122
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:13,480
You've already had
something work fast.

123
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:14,430
The ice.

124
00:03:14,570 --> 00:03:16,170
The first week of a new
pill.

125
00:03:16,210 --> 00:03:17,900
The good day after a
session.

126
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:19,220
Then it wore off.

127
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:21,370
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

128
00:03:21,410 --> 00:03:23,450
Fast relief isn't relief.

129
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:25,340
It's a preview.

130
00:03:25,730 --> 00:03:27,100
So I'm not going to tell

131
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:28,490
you this works fast.

132
00:03:28,530 --> 00:03:29,440
It doesn't.

133
00:03:29,730 --> 00:03:31,430
But if you're willing to
be patient,

134
00:03:31,430 --> 00:03:32,160
and to look at what's

135
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:33,540
going on around your new
knee

136
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:35,060
instead of inside it,
there

137
00:03:35,060 --> 00:03:37,040
is a real reason it still
hurts.

138
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:39,020
And something you can do
about it.

139
00:03:39,670 --> 00:03:41,320
Let me explain what he
said,

140
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,660
because this is what
changed

141
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:43,960
everything for me.

142
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,880
He started with the
basics.

143
00:03:46,070 --> 00:03:47,550
A knee replacement takes
out

144
00:03:47,550 --> 00:03:49,420
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

145
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:50,860
in metal and plastic.

146
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:52,690
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

147
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:54,430
you had before the
operation.

148
00:03:54,590 --> 00:03:56,270
That part I already knew.

149
00:03:56,350 --> 00:03:57,680
But then he explained
something

150
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:59,270
nobody had ever told me.

151
00:03:59,370 --> 00:04:00,160
He said,

152
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:01,360
think about a swollen foot

153
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,400
inside a shoe.

154
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:03,770
The shoe didn't shrink.

155
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:05,820
Your foot is taking up
more room,

156
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:07,340
so everything feels
cramped

157
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:08,970
and tight and squeezed.

158
00:04:09,510 --> 00:04:10,660
Your new knee sits

159
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:12,270
in a limited space with
living

160
00:04:12,270 --> 00:04:14,310
tissue packed all around
it.

161
00:04:14,410 --> 00:04:16,430
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

162
00:04:16,430 --> 00:04:18,220
had to work through that
tissue.

163
00:04:18,270 --> 00:04:21,000
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

164
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:23,260
At first that's normal.

165
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:24,450
But in some people

166
00:04:24,450 --> 00:04:25,870
that swelling can stay
switched

167
00:04:25,870 --> 00:04:27,810
on far longer than
expected.

168
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:29,510
And swollen tissue takes
up more

169
00:04:29,510 --> 00:04:31,370
room than calm tissue
does.

170
00:04:31,430 --> 00:04:33,850
So when you bend,

171
00:04:33,850 --> 00:04:35,320
that tissue gets
compressed.

172
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:36,500
When you straighten,

173
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:37,720
it gets pulled tight.

174
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:38,760
That's the band.

175
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:40,990
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

176
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:42,050
And you start being

177
00:04:42,050 --> 00:04:43,520
the one who says,

178
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:44,530
you go ahead.

179
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:45,860
I'll stay here.

180
00:04:45,970 --> 00:04:47,460
And that's exactly why so
much

181
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:49,440
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

182
00:04:50,010 --> 00:04:52,120
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

183
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:53,000
around the knee.

184
00:04:53,050 --> 00:04:53,980
Worth doing,

185
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:55,000
and I'd done it.

186
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,300
It does nothing about
tissue

187
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:57,410
taking up room.

188
00:04:57,580 --> 00:04:59,040
A nerve block quiets

189
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:00,820
the nerve carrying the
signal.

190
00:05:01,010 --> 00:05:03,200
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

191
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,640
But when that irritated
tissue

192
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:07,260
finally calms down,

193
00:05:07,260 --> 00:05:08,600
it holds less fluid,

194
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,470
and it takes up less room.

195
00:05:10,710 --> 00:05:11,880
Less room taken up means

196
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:13,930
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

197
00:05:14,190 --> 00:05:15,860
That's what takes the
pressure off.

198
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:17,560
After two years of this,

199
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:19,090
it finally made sense.

200
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:21,620
The problem was never the
new knee.

201
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:23,620
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

202
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:25,200
He calls it the squeeze.

203
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:27,460
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

204
00:05:27,550 --> 00:05:28,910
I'd bought knee sleeves,

205
00:05:28,910 --> 00:05:30,960
compression braces,
creams,

206
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:32,750
half of Amazon really,

207
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:34,460
and all any of it gave me

208
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:35,410
was an hour.

209
00:05:35,550 --> 00:05:36,550
I even looked at going

210
00:05:36,550 --> 00:05:38,470
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

211
00:05:38,550 --> 00:05:40,510
But at $200 a session

212
00:05:40,510 --> 00:05:42,340
with nothing covered by
insurance,

213
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:43,710
that was a quick no.

214
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:45,570
Then one night

215
00:05:45,570 --> 00:05:47,110
I went back to that knee
replacement

216
00:05:47,110 --> 00:05:48,940
group and actually read
it.

217
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:50,430
Thousands of people,

218
00:05:50,430 --> 00:05:52,010
years out from surgery,

219
00:05:52,010 --> 00:05:54,200
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

220
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:55,650
nobody could explain.

221
00:05:55,770 --> 00:05:57,700
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

222
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:59,370
the same thing kept coming
up.

223
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:01,020
This one device,

224
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:02,770
and people saying it was
the first

225
00:06:02,770 --> 00:06:04,350
thing that made a
difference.

226
00:06:04,450 --> 00:06:07,540
And before anyone jumps in
thinking, alright,

227
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:08,980
here it comes,

228
00:06:08,980 --> 00:06:10,500
she's selling me
something,

229
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:12,690
let me shut that down
right now.

230
00:06:12,730 --> 00:06:14,410
I'm only here because I
made myself

231
00:06:14,410 --> 00:06:16,440
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

232
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:17,460
that if I ever found

233
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:18,640
something that helped,

234
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:19,680
I'd say so.

235
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:22,040
It's called the KenRelief

236
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:23,580
Red Light Therapy Wrap.

237
00:06:24,190 --> 00:06:26,340
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

238
00:06:26,430 --> 00:06:28,060
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

239
00:06:28,060 --> 00:06:30,130
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

240
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:32,120
But I went to their
website anyway,

241
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:33,090
just to see what all

242
00:06:33,090 --> 00:06:34,230
the fuss was about.

243
00:06:34,330 --> 00:06:36,470
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

244
00:06:36,470 --> 00:06:38,980
charge $200 a session for,

245
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:41,660
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

246
00:06:41,660 --> 00:06:42,610
in a wrap you plug

247
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:43,910
into the wall at home.

248
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,600
Two hundred and forty
lights.

249
00:06:45,710 --> 00:06:47,910
Red at 660 nanometers

250
00:06:47,910 --> 00:06:50,460
and near-infrared at 850,

251
00:06:50,460 --> 00:06:52,570
run together for the
strongest effect.

252
00:06:52,710 --> 00:06:54,040
Four strength levels.

253
00:06:54,110 --> 00:06:55,960
A five to thirty minute
timer.

254
00:06:56,070 --> 00:06:57,560
Then I saw the guarantee.

255
00:06:57,640 --> 00:06:58,710
Ninety days.

256
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:00,720
Results or your money
back,

257
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:03,240
no questions, no store
credit,

258
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:04,850
and you don't even send it
back.

259
00:07:05,770 --> 00:07:07,730
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

260
00:07:07,730 --> 00:07:09,190
days to change my mind.

261
00:07:09,250 --> 00:07:10,330
There wasn't much to lose,

262
00:07:10,330 --> 00:07:11,530
so I ordered it.

263
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:13,020
Two of them, actually.

264
00:07:13,150 --> 00:07:14,900
Only the right knee was
replaced,

265
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:16,770
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

266
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:17,970
and I'd done it on every

267
00:07:17,970 --> 00:07:19,450
shift for two years.

268
00:07:20,030 --> 00:07:21,940
The left one was carrying
the difference.

269
00:07:22,050 --> 00:07:23,000
When it came,

270
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,130
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

271
00:07:25,130 --> 00:07:26,450
because I'd been let down
too

272
00:07:26,450 --> 00:07:28,000
many times to get excited.

273
00:07:28,230 --> 00:07:29,680
What I felt was warmth.

274
00:07:29,870 --> 00:07:31,760
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

275
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:33,440
More like it was coming
from inside

276
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:35,280
the knee and spreading
around it.

277
00:07:35,340 --> 00:07:36,530
And that was it.

278
00:07:36,570 --> 00:07:38,160
That was the whole
experience.

279
00:07:38,350 --> 00:07:39,500
When I took it off,

280
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:40,480
I'll be honest,

281
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,180
nothing dramatic had
happened.

282
00:07:42,290 --> 00:07:44,120
And after what that video
said,

283
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:45,960
that's exactly what I
expected.

284
00:07:46,050 --> 00:07:46,880
What was different

285
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:47,810
was that for the first

286
00:07:47,810 --> 00:07:49,220
time in two years

287
00:07:49,220 --> 00:07:50,740
I'd done something for my
knee

288
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:51,910
instead of to it.

289
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:53,580
Twenty minutes,

290
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:54,680
in my own chair,

291
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:55,600
after my shift.

292
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:57,400
No drive, no copay.

293
00:07:57,450 --> 00:07:58,760
They say twenty minutes.

294
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:00,390
I did thirty,

295
00:08:00,390 --> 00:08:01,440
twice a day,

296
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:03,040
lowest setting that first
week.

297
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:04,700
I put it on the calendar.

298
00:08:04,750 --> 00:08:05,710
The first week,

299
00:08:05,710 --> 00:08:06,450
I couldn't have told

300
00:08:06,450 --> 00:08:08,080
you if anything was
happening.

301
00:08:08,210 --> 00:08:09,090
I tried not to get

302
00:08:09,090 --> 00:08:10,060
my hopes up.

303
00:08:10,150 --> 00:08:11,000
I'd had things help

304
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,720
for a week and then stop.

305
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:13,990
But somewhere in the
second week

306
00:08:13,990 --> 00:08:15,090
I noticed I'd come down

307
00:08:15,090 --> 00:08:17,030
the stairs without holding
the rail.

308
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:18,680
I hadn't decided to.

309
00:08:18,730 --> 00:08:20,370
I just did it,

310
00:08:20,370 --> 00:08:22,100
then stopped halfway down

311
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:23,530
because I realized.

312
00:08:23,780 --> 00:08:25,300
By the end of the fourth
week

313
00:08:25,300 --> 00:08:26,330
I'd slept through the
night

314
00:08:26,330 --> 00:08:27,770
four times running.

315
00:08:27,900 --> 00:08:29,510
I stood at the counter and
finished

316
00:08:29,510 --> 00:08:31,620
making dinner without
looking for the stool.

317
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:33,140
None of that is dramatic.

318
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:34,160
All of it was gone

319
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:35,410
for two years.

320
00:08:35,470 --> 00:08:37,080
A few weeks later my
husband asked

321
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,000
if I wanted to walk

322
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,680
the long way around the
block.

323
00:08:39,950 --> 00:08:40,770
And for the first time

324
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:41,790
in two years,

325
00:08:41,790 --> 00:08:42,880
I said yes.

326
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:44,600
I wanted to understand
why,

327
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:46,040
so I read the whole thing.

328
00:08:46,230 --> 00:08:48,040
It comes down to four
steps.

329
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:48,810
One.

330
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:50,330
The tissue around a new
knee can

331
00:08:50,330 --> 00:08:52,940
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

332
00:08:53,570 --> 00:08:54,190
Two.

333
00:08:54,230 --> 00:08:56,450
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

334
00:08:56,450 --> 00:08:57,300
so it takes up more

335
00:08:57,300 --> 00:08:58,410
room than it should.

336
00:08:58,510 --> 00:08:59,170
Three.

337
00:08:59,210 --> 00:09:00,850
There's only so much room
in there.

338
00:09:00,890 --> 00:09:02,370
Bending compresses it.

339
00:09:02,410 --> 00:09:04,290
Straightening pulls it
tight.

340
00:09:04,990 --> 00:09:06,140
That's the squeeze.

341
00:09:06,270 --> 00:09:07,050
Four.

342
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:09,420
Red and near-infrared
light have been

343
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:11,760
studied for calming that
inflammation,

344
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,210
so the swelling and the
pressure

345
00:09:13,210 --> 00:09:14,600
can come down with it.

346
00:09:14,660 --> 00:09:16,470
In a randomized trial,

347
00:09:16,470 --> 00:09:18,380
patients given light
therapy after

348
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:20,650
a knee replacement had
less pain,

349
00:09:20,650 --> 00:09:22,520
less swelling and better
early

350
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:24,410
movement than those who
weren't.

351
00:09:24,910 --> 00:09:27,810
A 2025 review said the
same,

352
00:09:27,810 --> 00:09:29,290
and was clear the evidence

353
00:09:29,290 --> 00:09:30,480
is still limited.

354
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:32,070
I probably sound like a
broken

355
00:09:32,070 --> 00:09:33,470
record to my family

356
00:09:33,470 --> 00:09:35,090
and everyone on my floor.

357
00:09:35,170 --> 00:09:37,140
But after two years of
doing everything

358
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:39,230
I was told and getting
nowhere,

359
00:09:39,230 --> 00:09:40,750
you have no idea what it's
like

360
00:09:40,750 --> 00:09:42,060
to sleep through the
night,

361
00:09:42,060 --> 00:09:43,430
say yes to the walk,

362
00:09:43,430 --> 00:09:44,750
and get my life back.

363
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:46,540
So take it from me.

364
00:09:46,580 --> 00:09:47,940
Don't spend another year
waiting

365
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:48,970
for it to settle.

366
00:09:49,110 --> 00:09:51,190
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

367
00:09:51,230 --> 00:09:52,520
More than ten thousand
people

368
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:53,550
with pain after a knee

369
00:09:53,550 --> 00:09:55,760
replacement have already
tried this.

370
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:57,740
Some had it worse than I
did.

371
00:09:57,780 --> 00:09:58,960
You can get the KenRelief

372
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,510
